From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: Setting a window's pixel format again to the same one succeeds.

On Windows a window keeps the pixel format it was given first: setting the same format again succeeds and another one
fails. Wine's builtin opengl32 does this itself, but gdi32 hands SetPixelFormat to whichever opengl32 is loaded, and
Mesa's WGL, which is loaded natively here for the Zink path, refuses every second call on a window (DrvSetPixelFormat
returns false once the window has a framebuffer). A game that sets its window's format twice, as Godot 4 does in
window_create and again in _create_context, stopped at "Failed to create an OpenGL window". gdi32 now answers a repeated
call for the format the window already has before it reaches the driver; a different format still goes to the driver.

The problem was found by reading bornaradusin/PC5 (LGPL-2.1-or-later; patch 0066 (its Wine patch 0956) of its patches/prospero-win); this
change is written independently here (NOTICE.md, "PC5").
---
 dlls/gdi32/opengl.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/gdi32/opengl.c b/dlls/gdi32/opengl.c
index 0fbd851..1a2e4b6 100644
--- a/dlls/gdi32/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/opengl.c
@@ -92,6 +92,10 @@ BOOL WINAPI SetPixelFormat( HDC hdc, INT fmt, const PIXELFORMATDESCRIPTOR *pfd )
         if (!(wglSetPixelFormat = (void *)GetProcAddress( opengl32, "wglSetPixelFormat" )))
             return FALSE;
     }
+    /* On Windows a window keeps the format it was given first: setting the same one again succeeds, another fails.
+     * Mesa's WGL, which is the opengl32 here, refuses every second call. A game that sets its window's format twice
+     * (Godot 4 does, in window_create and again in _create_context) then found no OpenGL window. */
+    if (fmt > 0 && GetPixelFormat( hdc ) == fmt) return TRUE;
     return wglSetPixelFormat( hdc, fmt, pfd );
 }
 
